    "How far back (in tokens) the repetition penalty looks. Larger windows catch longer-range loops at a small decode-speed cost. Chat models rarely need more than 64; small/Q4 local models prone to JSON-template loops benefit from values ≥200 because a single tool-call envelope is ~60 tokens." : {

    },
    "How Gate Nodes Work" : {
      "comment" : "A title for a section that explains how gate nodes function within the workflow.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "How long Orb waits before deciding your command is finished. Speech recognition stops on its own after about 1.5 seconds of silence, so Quick is the shortest wait that has any effect." : {
      "comment" : "Description of the wait time after speaking.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "How many consecutive tool failures the agent tolerates before it gives up. Separate from the parse-failure setting above and from the policy below — this is the count; the policy decides what happens once the count is reached.\n\n• Auto: a sensible default (3)." : {

    },
    "How many times to resend with a correction hint when the LLM returns output the system can't parse (malformed JSON, missing fields). This affects ONLY parse failures.\n\n• Auto: a sensible default (3).\n• Higher counts help smaller/local models that parse less reliably.\n\nNetwork issues (timeouts, rate limits, server errors) are handled automatically based on your provider and are not configured here." : {

    },
