    "What you say to go ahead. Separate several with commas. Orb matches the whole phrase, so \"approve\" won't fire on \"don't approve that\"." : {

    },
    "What you say to skip it. A word listed in both places always denies — an ambiguous answer should never run a tool." : {

    },
    "When a tool execution fails repeatedly" : {

    },
    "When a tool execution fails repeatedly.\n\n• Abort: Stop immediately and report the error\n• Skip & Continue: Ignore the failed tool and keep reasoning\n• Fallback Prompt: Ask the LLM to find an alternative approach" : {

    },
    "When enabled, the agent **evaluates its own output** after completing a task. If the result isn't good enough, it retries with self-critique — learning from what went wrong." : {

    },
    "When enabled, the agent **generates a plan** (a list of subtasks) before acting. Each subtask runs its own ReAct loop, then results are synthesised into a final response." : {

    },
    "When enabled, the console logs the full prompt sent to the model, including the file contents and personal context it carries. This is live-console only — it is never written to disk or included in an exported diagnostic bundle. Developer Mode does not change what is stored: which logs are kept on disk is decided solely by Store Diagnostic Traces below." : {

    },
    "When enabled, the LLM response will appear word-by-word. Disable this if you prefer to receive the full response at once after it has been generated." : {

    },
    "When enabled, transcription will automatically finalize after detecting silence, allowing hands-free voice input." : {

    },
    "When max iterations are reached without completion" : {

    },
    "When ON, each subtask receives only the tools relevant to it, reducing LLM confusion. Recommended for agents with many tools." : {

    },
